‎
‎## 6. Operating Instruction for HakunaShortcut
‎
‎**When you feel:**
‎
‎- Information overload → Crossroads: believe or investigate?
‎- Opportunity appears → Crossroads: accept, reject, negotiate?
‎- New technology → Crossroads: adopt, adapt, remain dependent?
‎- System pressure → Crossroads: comply, navigate, build alternative?
‎- Life friction → Crossroads: continue, change, stop?
‎- Knowledge signal → Crossroads: observe, question, ignore?
‎
‎**Ask:**
‎
‎1. Have I reached a crossroads? (Make it visible)
‎2. What does non-decision cost here? (Name consequence)
‎3. What does evaluation reveal? (Use Checklist 01-13)
‎4. What choice do I want my life/system to reveal?
‎
‎> Make a Choice and decide what you want your life to be.
‎
‎**Because at crossroads, not choosing is also deciding what your life will be.**
